n-current focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-ring [&amp;_svg]:size-5 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0">More on<!-- --> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" aria-label="X"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18.25 15.25V5.75H8.75" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="square"></path><path d="M6 18L17.6002 6.39978" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="square"></path></svg></a></div></div><div class="voices" style="--voices-fold:42rem"><div class="rail-bare rail-column -mx-4 flex snap-x snap-mandatory gap-4 overflow-x-auto sm:mx-0 sm:snap-none sm:overflow-visible sm:px-0 mt-6 lg:mt-10 sm:block sm:columns-2 lg:columns-3"><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/alexfinn.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Alex Finn</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->AlexFinn<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 28</span></span><a href="https://x.com/AlexFinn/status/2093455057429889311" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Alex Finn on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">If you use AI, you need to switch to Omarchy immediately</span><span class="mt-2 block">It is an AI first, open source operating system by <a href="https://x.com/dhh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@dhh</a> and it has skyrocketed my productivity</span><span class="mt-2 block">In this video I cover how to use it, how to install it, and why I&#x27;m having more fun using computers than I ever have before:</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/alexfinn-2093455057429889311-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span><span class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center"><span class="flex size-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-black/55 text-white"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="ml-0.5 size-5"><path d="M5 22V2L22 12L5 22Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/ojisankaichou.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Ojisan Kaichou</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->OjisanKaichou<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 28</span></span><a href="https://x.com/OjisanKaichou/status/2093398890066137123" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Ojisan Kaichou on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">After 3 days I am confident in saying that Omarchy Quattro is the absolute best operating system I have ever used, hands down. Better than MacOS. Better than Ubuntu. Way better than Windows. </span><span class="mt-2 block">I never knew how much I wanted a tiling window manager until now. I never knew how slow everything else is until now. I didn&#x27;t know that computing could be as easy and enjoyable today as it was back in the Commodore 64 era. </span><span class="mt-2 block">It strikes the perfect balance between &quot;it just works&quot; and &quot;it works if you put in the effort.&quot; MacOS is the former, other Linux distros are the latter. The AI integration with Omarchy makes it easy to customize and fix any problems along the way with minimum friction and frustration. Doing everything with keyboard commands takes me back to the Windows 3 era when Windows was fun and not an evil overlord.</span><span class="mt-2 block">But I do know that I have only scratched the surface of what Omarchy has to offer. The future looks bright!</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/ojisankaichou-2093398890066137123-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/simonhoiberg.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Simon Høiberg</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->SimonHoiberg<!-- --> · <!-- -->Sep 1</span></span><a href="https://x.com/SimonHoiberg/status/2094771648377348264" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Simon Høiberg on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I&#x27;m officially installing Omarchy everywhere. This OS is just so good and it just doesn&#x27;t stop growing on me 🤌</span><span class="mt-2 block">Please create Omarchy Android, <a href="https://x.com/dhh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@dhh</a>. I want to go all-in!</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/simonhoiberg-2094771648377348264-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/gmgauthier1967.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Greg Gauthier</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->gmgauthier1967<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 30</span></span><a href="https://x.com/gmgauthier1967/status/2094121529042710854" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Greg Gauthier on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I will say this much about Omarchy: </span><span class="mt-2 block">I haven&#x27;t seen this kind of popular energy around an OPERATING SYSTEM, since Windows 95. </span><span class="mt-2 block">This definitely has that &quot;Where Do You Want To Go, Today?&quot; feel to it. </span><span class="mt-2 block"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wRdl1BjTG7c" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wRdl1BjTG7c</a></span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/markfenner.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Hybrid 🏃🏾</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->markfenner<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 21</span></span><a href="https://x.com/markfenner/status/2090847611414589575" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Hybrid 🏃🏾 on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I’ve been running Ubuntu on my second machine for over a decade.</span><span class="mt-2 block">After seeing another breakdown of Omarchy, this time from <a href="https://x.com/NetworkChuck" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@NetworkChuck</a>, I’m fully making the switch today.</span><span class="mt-2 block">He changed the entire desktop theme in seconds, used an AI agent to build a Quickshell plugin, handed a crashed process to the agent for diagnosis, ran games through Proton, and launched a Windows VM when Linux wasn’t enough.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Omarchy isn’t just Arch with a nice desktop.</span><span class="mt-2 block">It starts with Arch, Hyprland, Quickshell, and a keyboard-first workflow, then gives you an environment you can continue reshaping around how you work (the linux boys calls this ricing).</span><span class="mt-2 block">The operating system can become another surface your agents can help you modify.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Ubuntu had a great run.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Omarchy loading…</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/markfenner-2090847611414589575-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span><span class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center"><span class="flex size-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-black/55 text-white"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="ml-0.5 size-5"><path d="M5 22V2L22 12L5 22Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/ozolinsjanis.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Janis Ozolins</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->OzolinsJanis<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 28</span></span><a href="https://x.com/OzolinsJanis/status/2093410871682691205" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Janis Ozolins on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I&#x27;m enjoying the last dance with Mac OS. It&#x27;s been beautiful 15+ years. But I can&#x27;t resist this passion and energy around Omarchy. I&#x27;ve never seen myself running Linux, as a non-dev, but times have changed.</span><span class="mt-2 block">As a vibe-coding fanatic for the past year, it’s a no-brainer to switch to an OS where agents are first-class citizens and where customizing the OS is natural, unlike in Mac where it’s a bit of an uphill battle.</span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/typecraft_dev.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">typecraft</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->typecraft_dev<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 29</span></span><a href="https://x.com/typecraft_dev/status/2093756974819098946" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by typecraft on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">FWIW no one paid me to make a video about omarchy. I actually love it</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/typecraft_dev-2093756974819098946-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/ironcladdev.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">IroncladDev</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->IroncladDev<!-- --> · <!-- -->Sep 4</span></span><a href="https://x.com/IroncladDev/status/2095890742547775752" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by IroncladDev on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">Omarchy unintentionally gave birth to a new design system that doesn&#x27;t just follow the standardized UI patterns on mainstream operating systems, and it&#x27;s beautiful</span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/oldstackjournal.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Lars Jansen</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->oldstackjournal<!-- --> · <!-- -->Sep 1</span></span><a href="https://x.com/oldstackjournal/status/2094728212064723139" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Lars Jansen on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I finally looked into Omarchy and I can see why dev twitter is suddenly obsessed with it.</span><span class="mt-2 block">It’s basically Arch with somebody else making all the hard/endless decisions for you.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Hyprland. Terminal first. Keyboard driven. Neovim. Plain config files. Very little “click through six settings panels and hope for the best”</span><span class="mt-2 block">This style of OS makes a lot of sense now with ai. An agent can read the config, edit the config, install the package , restart he service, inspect the logs and change the workflow.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Which is weird because the future of ai computing might end up looking a lot like the old way of using computers: files, terminals, scripts, text and a machine you can actually understand.</span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/etroll.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Karl Løland</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->etroll<!-- --> · <!-- -->Sep 1</span></span><a href="https://x.com/etroll/status/2094860150960013634" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Karl Løland on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">Using Omarchy for a week now, and needed the ability to mirror my screen to and AppleTV at the office (and home) for some presentation. Within ~30 mins, a plugin that can mirror screen and windows from Omarchy was created. The malleable computer from <a href="https://x.com/dhh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@dhh</a> is the future happening in front of our eyes.</span><span class="mt-2 block"><a href="https://github.com/ETroll/omarchy-airplay" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="break-all relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">https://github.com/ETroll/omarchy-airplay</a></span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/etroll-2094860150960013634-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/anushelangovan.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Anush Elangovan</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->AnushElangovan<!-- --> · <!-- -->Sep 5</span></span><a href="https://x.com/AnushElangovan/status/2096066455494435010" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Anush Elangovan on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">35s Omarchy install on my Halo laptop. Great work <a href="https://x.com/dhh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@dhh</a> . This is now my daily driver. Still getting used to the short cuts but the best Linux desktop to date (close to my custom Gentoo build that ofcourse took a few weeks to dial in😝)</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/anushelangovan-2096066455494435010-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/bias_micah.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Micah Bias</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->bias_micah<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 30</span></span><a href="https://x.com/bias_micah/status/2094034865670783032" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Micah Bias on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">Installed Omarchy. I don’t think I’m going back to windows for my personal daily driver. About an hour getting used to the tile navigation, and I’m hooked. So far, everything I’ve needed to install has been a few keystrokes away, and it all just works. This is wonderful.</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/bias_micah-2094034865670783032-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/fredimachado.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Fredi Machado</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->fredimachado<!-- --> · <!-- -->Sep 6</span></span><a href="https://x.com/fredimachado/status/2096526392012009955" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Fredi Machado on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I&#x27;m having so much fun with Omarchy. I&#x27;m having that sense of childlike wonder with this thing. I love it! I even built a dead-simple IRC client (Omairc) for it, because why not? Thanks <a href="https://x.com/dhh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@dhh</a> !! #omarchy</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/fredimachado-2096526392012009955-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/chshersh.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Dmitrii Kovanikov</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->ChShersh<!-- --> · <!-- -->Sep 6</span></span><a href="https://x.com/ChShersh/status/2096497679924678687" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Dmitrii Kovanikov on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I&#x27;ve been using Omarchy for a week, and here&#x27;s my full honest review.</span><span class="mt-2 block">It&#x27;s an OS that made me excited about computers again.</span><span class="mt-2 block">I was planning to play with it for only a couple of hours. But I find myself spending more and more time using it. It&#x27;s so pleasant to use that I don&#x27;t want to go back.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Omarchy is a chef&#x27;s special. And you can say that all the ingredients, like Arch, Hyprland, OpenCode, etc., existed long before, so you could always make it for yourself (not really true; people have built some things specifically for Omarchy from scratch). But someone spending so much time and resources to package everything nicely makes a big difference.</span><span class="mt-2 block">The fact that a fully working Omarchy setup is just a couple of minutes away makes a big difference. I can literally install it while I&#x27;m brewing my coffee and simply start using it immediately.</span><span class="mt-2 block">It just works ™️</span><span class="mt-2 block">And then I can spend all the time in the world tinkering with it because it&#x27;s such a nice experience.</span><span class="mt-2 block">You can notice that Omarchy is built by a person who cares about a product. It&#x27;s not just tech supremacism. Every minor detail matters, and every papercut is taken seriously.</span><span class="mt-2 block">As it should be.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Even an innocent tiny thing like &quot;pressing an arrow or backspace key moves the cursor a little bit faster&quot; makes a big difference for me. I do feel like the computer matches my speed of thinking and working.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Omarchy is not perfect. I had a minor issue with copy/paste keybindings with multiple language layouts (there&#x27;s an open PR to address that already, and my agent fixed it for me locally). Terminal and browser windows take several noticeable seconds to start on my old laptop in a power-saving mode. My agent broke my theme once when I was trying to be too experimental with it (but then it easily reverted it to a working state).</span><span class="mt-2 block">But honestly, this is nothing compared to how bad Windows and macOS can be in areas that matter.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Omarchy will get better. Substantial resources are put into it, and I trust the <a href="https://x.com/DHH" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@DHH</a> vision to make it even better.</span><span class="mt-2 block">My biggest genie wish for now is having a better file browser, e.g. a TUI version of Total Commander or Far Manager style. But I&#x27;ve already seen someone working on a similar thing, so I have high hopes.</span><span class="mt-2 block">I just can&#x27;t believe my oldest and least powerful laptop in my home is the machine I&#x27;m the most excited to use.</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/chshersh-2096497679924678687-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/ravivasavan.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Ravi Vasavan</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->ravivasavan<!-- --> · <!-- -->Sep 6</span></span><a href="https://x.com/ravivasavan/status/2096516934561079528" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Ravi Vasavan on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">Installed Omarchy on my PC, went as far as wiping any traces of Windows from it. It truly is opinionated and I love that agents are considered native, setting it up has been fun and plugging in all of my go-to&#x27;s were super easy. Hats off to <a href="https://x.com/dhh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@dhh</a> and all involved.</span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/predkelis.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Elvinas Predkelis</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->predkelis<!-- --> · <!-- -->Jul 2</span></span><a href="https://x.com/predkelis/status/1940338942232170504" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Elvinas Predkelis on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">All right, Omarchy is quite something. </span><span class="mt-2 block">It&#x27;s been a while back since I&#x27;ve last used Linux as a daily driver. But Omarchy is a breeze - snappy, intuitive and a joy to use.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Some personal tweaks here and there, adding Ghostty and it&#x27;s a dream machine. </span><span class="mt-2 block">Thank you <a href="https://x.com/dhh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whitespace-nowrap relative z-20 text-text underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 ease-out hover:decoration-brand">@dhh</a> 🙏</span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/l0gicgate.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">l0gicgate</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->l0gicgate<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 30</span></span><a href="https://x.com/l0gicgate/status/2094207064033935449" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by l0gicgate on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I was using Manjaro and almost everything was broken in the distro. </span><span class="mt-2 block">Omarchy just works out of the box and is more polished than other distros out there. </span><span class="mt-2 block">Also wanted hyprland already setup for me. Been mainlining it for 425 days now. Love it.</span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/d_av_id_.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface