2. Omarchy runs circles around macOS itself on this machine, which had become entirely unusable</span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/brodieonlinux.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Brodie Robertson</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->BrodieOnLinux<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 31</span></span><a href="https://x.com/BrodieOnLinux/status/2094441549082017881" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Brodie Robertson on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">It is funny to me how much mental energy is being spent trying to find vulnerabilities in Omarchy as a dunk on the project inadvertently making it way more secure than it would have been if left alone.</span></p></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/lundukejournal.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">The Lunduke Journal</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->LundukeJournal<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 24</span></span><a href="https://x.com/LundukeJournal/status/2091724230035488984" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by The Lunduke Journal on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505 10.6628L21.6753 20.75H15.7052L11.0291 14.6322L5.67867 20.75H2.71017L9.64264 12.8212L2.32812 3.25H8.44986L12.6766 8.84192L17.5652 3.25ZM16.524 18.9731H18.1679L7.55662 4.93359H5.79256L16.524 18.9731Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></a></header><p class="line-clamp-6 font-sans text-[15px] leading-snug whitespace-pre-line text-text-secondary [text-wrap:pretty]"><span class="block">I see a lot of activists attacking Omarchy Linux for getting $8 Million in donations to fund its new Foundation.</span><span class="mt-2 block">“Omarchy is compromised!”, they exclaim.  “It’s for billionaires… it’s not for the people!  It’s Oligarchy Linux.”</span><span class="mt-2 block">This is, quite frankly, retarded.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Who funds Fedora?  IBM (and their multi-billion dollar subsidiary, Red Hat).</span><span class="mt-2 block">Who funds the Linux kernel?  Microsoft, Meta, Amazon, IBM, and a bunch of other Billion dollar corporations (often run by billionaires).  All directly funding and controlling a quarter billion dollar per year trade organization.</span><span class="mt-2 block">If “Omarchy is compromised… it’s Oligarchy Linux!”… then so is Fedora.  And absolutely every system which uses the Linux kernel.  Without exception.</span><span class="mt-2 block">Yet we see this “3 generations of inbreeding” level of stupid being spouted all across Mastodon.</span></p><span class="relative block overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><span class="block aspect-video"><img src="/assets/images/voices/lundukejournal-2091724230035488984-1.webp" alt="" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="img-outlined size-full object-cover "/></span></span></article></div><div class="w-full shrink-0 snap-center sm:contents"><article class="ring-elevation ring-elevation-hover group relative mb-4 flex w-full flex-col break-inside-avoid gap-4 rounded-xl bg-surface p-6"><header class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src="/assets/images/voices/dhoesq.webp" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-2 object-cover"/><span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col leading-tight"><span class="truncate text-sm font-medium text-text">Don Ho, Esq.</span><span class="truncate font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">@<!-- -->dhoesq<!-- --> · <!-- -->Aug 30</span></span><a href="https://x.com/dhoesq/status/2094008751972040929" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the post by Don Ho, Esq. on X" class="ml-auto flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center text-text-muted transition-colors duration-150 ease-out group-hover:text-text before:absolute before:inset-0 before:z-10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="size-5"><path d="M17.5652 3.25H20.5319L14.0505